# Local Interconnect Network (LIN) network layer core configuration
#

menuconfig LIN
	tristate "LIN bus subsystem support"
	help
	  Local Interconnect Network (LIN) is a low-cost, single-master
	  serial bus widely used in automotive body electronics for
	  subsystems where CAN is oversized — door modules, window lifts,
	  seat controls, and similar. It is specified by ISO 17987.

	  This option enables the PF_LIN protocol family, which provides
	  socket-based access to LIN network interfaces following the same
	  model as SocketCAN (PF_CAN). Select this if you want to build
	  the LIN core; you will also need a driver for your specific
	  LIN controller under the Network device support section.

if LIN

config LIN_RAW
	tristate "Raw LIN Protocol (frame-level access with ID filtering)"
	default y
	help
	  The raw LIN protocol offers access to a LIN bus via the BSD
	  socket API. Applications exchange struct lin_frame with the
	  kernel and configure subscribe filters, publisher ownership,
	  master-role claim, and master schedules via setsockopt(). To
	  send or receive raw LIN frames, use AF_LIN with protocol LIN_RAW.

endif
